5 716 M
(Related Works) s
5 694 M
(Color histograms have long been used to index images. They are very easy ) s
5 683 M
(to compute and have proven useful. However, the problem with color ) s
5 672 M
(histograms is that they do not include any spatial information of colors ) s
5 661 M
(and thus are very liable to false positives. Besides, when there is a ) s
5 650 M
(large appearance change in the image \(such as adding borders\), the color ) s
5 639 M
(histograms will have difficulty finding the similarity between the image ) s
5 628 M
(and the changed image.) s
5 606 M
(Several methods have been proposed to modify the color histograms. Pass ) s
5 595 M
(and Zabih [1,2] use the color coherence vector\(CCV\) which partitions each ) s
5 584 M
(color into a coherent portion and an incoherent portion. CCV is easy to ) s
5 573 M
(compute and has been shown to work better than the color histograms. But ) s
5 562 M
(it is still very vulnerable to such appearance changes as adding borders ) s
5 551 M
(or frames. Hsu et al. [3] selects a set of dominant colors and then ) s
5 540 M
(partitions the image into rectangular regions so that each region mainly ) s
5 529 M
(contains one color. The similarity of two images is then determined by ) s
5 518 M
(the degree of overlap between regions of the same color. Smith and Chang ) s
5 507 M
([4] use a different algorithm to partition the image into regions. ) s
5 496 M
(Employing histogram back-projection [5],  they allow  one region to have ) s
5 485 M
(multiple different colors and the colors of each region are represented ) s
5 474 M
(by a binary color set. The binary color sets and their location ) s
5 463 M
(information combined is the feature vector for an image. This feature ) s
5 452 M
(vector can facilitate the region queries. Huang et al. [6,7] tries to ) s
5 441 M
(encode the spatial correlation of color-bin pairs by the "color ) s
5 430 M
(correlogram". These approaches usually can give a better result than ) s
5 419 M
(color histograms. Nevertheless, they \(esp. the ones involving image ) s
5 408 M
(partition\) are much more difficult to compute and often require more ) s
5 397 M
(storage space for the feature vectors than the color histograms. ) s
5 375 M
(Our approach tries to find an efficient way to incorporate the spatial ) s
5 364 M
(information of the colors into the feature of images. We introduce the ) s
5 353 M
(variances of the colors into the feature vector. The variances of the ) s
5 342 M
(colors are overall indicators about how the colors are spatially ) s
5 331 M
(distributed in the images. Combining the variance and the number of ) s
5 320 M
(pixels of each color, we compose the color variance vector\(CVV\). The CVV ) s
5 309 M
(is very easy to compute. In fact, it can be computed in a single pass ) s
5 298 M
(over the image. CVV is especially effective and efficient in finding the ) s
5 287 M
(similarity between the image and the image with a border or frame because ) s
5 276 M
(of the special properties of the variance. It can identify the cropped ) s
5 265 M
(versions of the image with the original one very easily. CVV can also ) s
5 254 M
(serve as a general-purposed feature vector in the image retrieval system.) s
5 188 M
(1. G. Pass, R. Zabih and J. Miller. Comparing Images Using Color ) s
5 177 M
(Coherence Vectors, Proceedings of the Fourth ACM Multimedia Conference, ) s
5 166 M
(pages 65-73,1996. ) s
5 144 M
(2. G. Pass and R. Zabih. Histogram refinement for content-based image ) s
5 133 M
(retrieval. IEEE Workshop on Applications of Computer Vision, pages ) s
5 122 M
(96-102, 1996.) s
5 100 M
(3. Wynne Hsu, T. S. Chua, and H. K. Pung. An integrated color-spatial ) s
5 89 M
(approach to content-based image retrieval. ACM Multimedia Conference, ) s
5 78 M
(pages 305-313, 1995.) s
5 56 M
(4. J. Smith and S-F Chang. Tools and techniques for color image ) s
5 45 M
(retrieval. SPIE proceedings, 2670:1630-1639, 1996.) s
5 23 M
(5. Michael Swain and Dana Ballard. Color Indexing. International Journal ) s
5 12 M
(of Computer Vision , 7\(1\):11-32, 1991.   ) s
_R
